testcase.name:
[PR-J J1] 5. invalid hierarchies refuse with named diagnostics and resolve to no nets > a sheet pin naming a port that does not exist -> (state) => {
      state.netLabels[0].portId = "p-nope";
    }

[PR-J J1] 5. invalid hierarchies refuse with named diagnostics and resolve to no nets > a hierarchical label on the wrong sheet -> (state) => {
      delete state.netLabels[1].sheetId;
    }

[PR-J J1] 5. invalid hierarchies refuse with named diagnostics and resolve to no nets > a sheet pin that is not on the child's parent -> (state) => {
      state.sheets.sheets.push(sheet("s2", "Other", (0,__vite_ssr_import_5__.ROOT_SHEET_ID)));
      state.netLabels[0].sheetId = "s2";
    }

[PR-J J1] 5. invalid hierarchies refuse with named diagnostics and resolve to no nets > two sheet pins for one port (conflicting bindings) -> (state) => {
      state.netLabels.push(label("pin-2", "SIG", { x: 500, y: 500 }, { scope: "sheet-pin", portId: "p-sig", childSheetId: "adc" }));
    }

[PR-J J1] 5. invalid hierarchies refuse with named diagnostics and resolve to no nets > a parent cycle -> (state) => {
      state.sheets.sheets.push(sheet("x1", "X1", "x2"), sheet("x2", "X2", "x1"));
    }

[PR-J J1] 5. invalid hierarchies refuse with named diagnostics and resolve to no nets > two roots -> (state) => {
      state.sheets.sheets.push(sheet("r2", "Second root", null));
    }

[PR-J J1] 5. invalid hierarchies refuse with named diagnostics and resolve to no nets > an entity on an unknown sheet -> (state) => {
      state.components[0].sheetId = "nowhere";
    }

[PR-J J1] 5. invalid hierarchies refuse with named diagnostics and resolve to no nets > an entity that stores the root id -> (state) => {
      state.components[0].sheetId = __vite_ssr_import_5__.ROOT_SHEET_ID;
    }

[PR-J J1] 5. invalid hierarchies refuse with named diagnostics and resolve to no nets > a missing parent -> (state) => {
      state.sheets.sheets.push(sheet("orphan", "Orphan", "gone"));
    }

[PR-J J1] 5. invalid hierarchies refuse with named diagnostics and resolve to no nets > two sibling sheets with one name -> (state) => {
      state.sheets.sheets.push(sheet("adc2", "adc", (0,__vite_ssr_import_5__.ROOT_SHEET_ID)));
    }

[PR-J J1] 5. invalid hierarchies refuse with named diagnostics and resolve to no nets > a bus port name -> (state) => {
      state.sheets.sheets[1].ports.push({ id: "p-bus", name: "DATA[0..7]", direction: "input" });
    }

[PR-J J1] 5. invalid hierarchies refuse with named diagnostics and resolve to no nets > a bundle port field -> (state) => {
      state.sheets.sheets[1].ports[0].members = ["D0", "D1"];
    }

[PR-J J1] 5. invalid hierarchies refuse with named diagnostics and resolve to no nets > a repeated sheet instance -> (state) => {
      state.sheets.sheets[1].instanceOf = "adc";
    }

[PR-J J1] 5. invalid hierarchies refuse with named diagnostics and resolve to no nets > one package's units split across sheets -> (state) => {
      state.kicadComponents = [{ id: "u1", partId: "p", x: 0, y: 0, rotation: 0, refDes: "U1", value: "x", unitPlacements: [{ unit: 2, sheetId: "adc" }] }];
    }

[PR-J J1] 5. invalid hierarchies refuse with named diagnostics and resolve to no nets > a port on the root sheet -> (state) => {
      state.sheets.sheets[0].ports = [{ id: "p-root", name: "X", direction: "input" }];
    }

[PR-J J1] 5. invalid hierarchies refuse with named diagnostics and resolve to no nets > two ports with one name on a sheet -> (state) => {
      state.sheets.sheets[1].ports.push({ id: "p-sig-2", name: "sig", direction: "output" });
    }

[PR-J J1] 5. invalid hierarchies refuse with named diagnostics and resolve to no nets > a power label with a scope -> (state) => {
      state.netLabels.push(label("pw", "+5V", { x: 0, y: 0 }, { kind: "power", scope: "global" }));
    }

[PR-J J1] 5. invalid hierarchies refuse with named diagnostics and resolve to no nets > a sheet tree with only the root -> (state) => {
      state.sheets = tree();
      state.components = state.components.filter((item) => !item.sheetId);
      state.wires = state.wires.filter((item) => !item.sheetId);
      state.netLabels = [];
    }

[SEC-1] model text is multi-line by nature: the final deck screen holds what the model screen misses > an empty transformedContent over a hostile originalContent (the screen reads one, the deck emits the other): the executed deck is refused by the final screen on its own (the model screen (model) => {
      model.originalContent = hostile([".control", `shell ${MARK}`, ".endc"]);
      model.transformedContent = "";
    } it)

[SEC-1] model text is multi-line by nature: the final deck screen holds what the model screen misses > a '*#' line (ngspice runs it as a control command): the executed deck is refused by the final screen on its own (the model screen (model) => {
      model.originalContent = hostile([`*# shell ${MARK}`]);
    } it)

[SEC-1] model text is multi-line by nature: the final deck screen holds what the model screen misses > a relative .include with no recorded dependency: the executed deck is refused by the final screen on its own (the model screen (model) => {
      model.originalContent = hostile([`.include ../../${MARK}.lib`]);
    } it)

[SEC-1] model text is multi-line by nature: the final deck screen holds what the model screen misses > a .lib read: the executed deck is refused by the final screen on its own (the model screen (model) => {
      model.originalContent = hostile([`.lib /${MARK}.lib tt`]);
    } it)
